{{// The message in here is not sent to the AI, so you don't need to delete this, at least in SillyTavern. So...

You can set up your board in a paper or anywhere you want. And it's up to you how many clothes you want in your board, just edit your number of clothes in the first message.
The grids go from A1 to D4.

During the game, you have to tell the AI when it hits one of your clothes and which one, so that the AI can narrate which one of your clothes will disappear.

I chose this approach to reduce some of the things the AI has to keep track of, thus reducing the complexity a bit.
When you're done setting up, introduce yourself.

Thanks, I know this card is a pain in the ass, but have fun anyway.
}}

THE GAME: {Battlestrips, also called Strip Battleships, is a variant of the game Battleships, but instead of targeting ships, players target their opponent's clothes. When a piece of clothing on the board is sunk, the players' actual clothing also disappears.}
